    } 
    Annotation {
      Name          "<html><body>\n<p><span style=\" font-weight:700;\">1. Bla"
"ck Start in an Open Circuit (Enable_1 = 1):</span></p></body></html>"
      Position      [1570, 135]
    } 
    Annotation {
      Name          "<html><body>\n<p>At the Point of Common Coupling (PCC), t"
"he dVCO is expected to generate a sinusoidal voltage waveform </p>\n<p>in eac"
"h phase with a peak amplitude close to (V_baseFNPeak. Due to the gainintroduc"
"ed by the LCL filter, </p>\n<p>the actual peak amplitude exhibits a slight ov"
"ervoltage of approximately 0.92%. Frequency is given by fg<span style=\" font"
"-weight:600;\">  </span></p></body></html>"
      Position      [1725, 170]
    } 
    RectangleAnnotation {
      Position     [2310, 380]
      Width        590
      Height       530
      CornerRadius 3
      Thickness    2
      PenColor     4294901760
      PenAlpha     1
      BrushColor   0
      BrushAlpha   0
    } 
    Annotation {
      Name          "<html><body>\n<p><span style=\" font-weight:700;\">2. Gri"
"d Connection with synchronization (Enable_2 = 1):</span></p></body></html>"
      Position      [2180, 135]
    } 
    Annotation {
      Name          "<html><body>\n<p><span style=\" font-weight:600;\">Valida"
"tes the transition from islanded to grid-connection operation. Additions to t"
"he dVOC not present</span></p>\n<p><span style=\" font-weight:600;\">in the p"
"aper</span></p></body></html>"
      Position      [2295, 170]
    } 
    Annotation {
      Name          "<html><body>\n<p><span style=\" font-weight:700;\">4. Gri"
"d disturbance and inverter support (enable_4 = 1), SCR = 3:</span></p>\n<p><s"
"pan style=\" font-weight:700; font-style:italic;\">Timeline </span></p>\n<p>0"
".50 s   Rload1 (30 MW) connects;  P* = 29 MW</p>\n<p>0.90 s   Pre-synchroniza"
"tion ON</p>\n<p>1.50 s   Grid breaker closes</p>\n<p>2.50 s   Voltage sag 30 "
"pct, 0.4 s  -&gt; ends at 2.90 s      [sag_en = 1]</p>\n<p>4.00 s   Frequency"
" step -0.2 Hz, permanent                      [freq_en = 1]</p>\n<p>5.20 s   "
"Phase jump +10 deg, 0.4 s                              [phase_en = 0, OFF]</p"
">\n<p>5.50 s   End of simulation  (7.00 s when phase_en = 1)</p>\n<p> </p>\n<"
"p><span style=\" font-weight:700; font-style:italic;\">V / pu : </span>V_grid"
"_cmd is the commanded source EMF, rebuilt from t_sag / dur_sag / V_sag. </p>"
"\n<p>The gap between it and V_PCC IS the grid-forming voltage support. V_osc "
"is the oscillator </p>\n<p>internal node, which sits above both. </p>\n<p><sp"
"an style=\" font-weight:700; font-style:italic;\">I / pu :</span><span style="
"\" font-style:italic;\"> </span>the sag inrush scales as sag_depth / X_pu. It"
" is important to mention that there's </p>\n<p>NO current limiter in this mod"
"el.</p>\n<p><span style=\" font-weight:700; font-style:italic;\">f / Hz :</sp"
"an><span style=\" font-style:italic;\"> </span>fixed axis 48.5 to 51.5 Hz on "
"purpose. </p>\n<p><span style=\" font-weight:700; font-style:italic;\">Q / pu"
" :</span><span style=\" font-weight:700;\"> </span>reactive support during th"
"e sag. </p></body></html>"
      Position      [2260, 790]
    } 
